          "court": "Supreme Court of North Carolina",
          "year": 2005,
          "date_decided": "2005-07-01",
          "holding": "The Supreme Court held that a trial court retains jurisdiction to enter an order terminating parental rights while an appeal of a custody order in the same juvenile case is pending, rejecting the Court of Appeals' contrary rule and explaining that N.C.G.S. § 7B-1003 expands rather than limits trial court jurisdiction in child custody proceedings.",
          "relevance": "It confirms the trial court's continuing jurisdiction to modify or vacate custody orders in light of changed circumstances or the juvenile's needs, the mechanism by which a case continues toward or past permanency.",
          "quote": "we hold a trial court retains jurisdiction to terminate parental rights during the pendency of a custody order appeal in the same case",
